# 118 - aegis-desktop-dark-theme (r60 wave, user feedback 2026-11-13)
# The desktop dark theme used Chromium's Google greys (#202124 frame,
# #35363A toolbar, #292A2D surfaces); the proposal specifies true black
# and a calibrated grey ramp (Table 5: bg #0A0A0B, surface #141416).
#
#   ui/color/core_default_color_mixer.cc:
#     kColorPrimaryBackground (dialog/bubble/WebUI base) dark
#       #292A2D -> #141416 (aegis surface)
#   ui/color/ui_color_mixer.cc:
#     kColorFrameActiveUnthemed dark kGoogleGrey900 #202124 -> #0A0A0B
#       (aegis bg - window frame + tab strip)
#     kColorFrameInactive dark kGoogleGrey800 #3C3F43 -> #141416
#   chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.cc:
#     kColorToolbar dark #35363A -> #141416 (toolbar, omnibox, bookmark
#     bar, side panel and infobars all derive from this)
# Text colors (GetColorWithMaxContrast / kGoogleGrey200) keep working:
# contrast ratios IMPROVE against the darker surfaces.
